
    TransAmigaConfig 
        - A program to configure TransAmiga BBS (c) Timothy Aston


    Introduction:
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    TransAmiga BBS is an excellent BBS program but I found that the configuration editor that comes with the package (TransConfig) is quite difficult to use. If a mistake was made, the entire configuration process had to be done again. If a single message or file area was to be added, again the entire configuration process had to be completed. Now with TransAmigaConfig, it is all controlled from a GUI making configuration a breeze.


    System Requirements:
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    TransAmigaConfig requires version 2.0x+ of the operation system. It uses certain capabilities that only 2.0x+ have. So if you have version 1.3, it will not work. TransAmigaConfig should run in 512k of ram. I have not tested this out but since the program is fairly small and I have 3 megs... Also for this program to be useful, you have to be running TransAmiga BBS.


    Disclaimer:
    ~~~~~~~~~~~
    TransAmigaConfig has been tested as thoroughly as possible on an Amiga2000, non-accelerated. I have found no bugs whatsoever. However if this program causes any problem at all on your computer, I will take no responsibility for any damages.
    TransAmigaConfig is shareware. It may be distributed by any BBS or on floppy disk as long as there are no monetary charges to anyone (except for the cost of the disk it is copied to).
